msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Building the names break audio sets these for you, and with the simple names"
" break each name gets the time it needs by itself. Change them only for your"
" own names sequence, to match where its audio goes quiet."
msgstr ""

msgid "Most names per break"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Names that need longer to read already get fewer, longer turns by "
"themselves. Pick a lower number to keep breaks short; any extra names go up "
"in the next break."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"With the simple names break Marquee makes for you, your FPP plays the break "
"itself: the intro, then each name for as long as it takes to read and say, "
"then the outro. One name makes a short break, six a longer one. With your "
"own names sequence, a shorter break plays when only 1 or 2 names are "
"waiting. Everything is set to the same loudness as your songs, so nobody has"
" to touch the radio volume."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your names break playlists already play audio you made, with your own "
"announcer. Marquee leaves it alone. Enter when your intro talking ends and "
"when the announcer starts again (below): names are only said in between, "
"never over your announcer. Turn this off to use the audio built here."
